+# Export acceptance and restart recovery hunt
+
+Date: 2026-10-24. Source revision: `dbfe2590f87964dae5c5b437db11c6c2cb29868f`.
+
+## Findings
+
+No implementation bug found within the supported operation and recovery path.
+This is a bounded hunt, not a proof of all executions.
+
+The oracle is [app/export-contract.md](app/export-contract.md): accepted jobs
+eventually produce their fixed payload after recovery, with one worker,
+non-overlapping requests, durable committed SQLite transactions, and retries
+after transient failures. Storage loss and database corruption are excluded.
+
+In [Queue.submit](app/export_queue.py), the job transaction commits before
+acceptance returns (lines 22–26). An interruption before commit does not create
+an acknowledged obligation; an interruption after commit retains the job even
+if the caller has not received the response. Same-payload resubmission does not
+replace or reset an existing job.
+
+`Queue.work` commits `running` before the instrumentation hook (lines 34–37).
+The job remains selectable even without restart; `Queue.recover` also resets
+`running` to `pending` on construction (lines 17–20). Result insertion and the
+`done` transition share one transaction (lines 38–40): interruption before its
+commit leaves retryable work, while interruption after commit leaves a result
+and a completed job excluded from selection. No process-local slot or separate
+acknowledgment can discard the durable obligation in this path.
+
+## Executable coverage
+
+Run: `python3 tests/hunt_witness.py`.
+
+Observed: **6 tests passed; exit status 0**. The witness uses production `Queue`
+with temporary local databases. Assertions or unexpected errors yield nonzero.
+Subprocess crashes use `os._exit(73)` without closing the connection, and the
+parent checks that exact exit code before examining recovery.
+
+| Check | Boundary and oracle |
+| --- | --- |
+| Accepted job | Exit immediately after acceptance; reopen and produce payload. |
+| Interrupted claim | Exit at the documented hook; confirm durable `running`, reopen and finish. |
+| Interrupted output transaction | SQLite trace callback exits before the `done` update (after result insertion), and separately before COMMIT (after both writes); reopen, finish, retain exactly one result. |
+| Completed job | Exit after successful work; reopen, retain result, perform no further work. |
+| Transient output failure | Temporary SQLite trigger aborts result insertion; remove fault, retry in the same process, then restart and confirm completion. |
+| Duplicate submission | Repeat the same ID and payload before and after completion; retain one result without new work. |
+
+The output-failure trigger checks rollback and retry control flow; it does not
+simulate every operating-system I/O error. The crash checks cover selected real
+SQL boundaries, not every instruction or recovery interruption. Recovery's reset
+is itself transactional: an interrupted reset leaves either `running` or
+`pending`, both selectable by the worker. This last observation is code inspection,
+not a separate crash test. Eventual completion assumes the contract's recovered
+environment and repeated work calls; the tests use finite retry bounds.
+
+## Scope and preservation
+
+Reviewed `Queue.__init__`, `submit`, `work`, `recover`, `result`, and their SQLite
+state transitions. Checked root record applicability and references: local-only
+storage applies; the note-payload specification concerns the separate
+`handler`/`exporter` path; import metadata requirements do not govern this queue.
+The single-writer claim concerns `data/` and `Store.write`; this hunt uses separate
+temporary queue databases and does not verify that claim or read its existing
+proof/verification reports. No queue-specific governing record was found.
+
+Stopped after this operation and recovery path. Concurrent workers, overlapping
+requests, changing a job's payload, storage loss, database corruption, unrelated
+note operations, and claim verification were not investigated. Product code,
+governing records, and existing evidence were preserved. Only this report and
+`tests/hunt_witness.py` were added.
